name w4-02-overcast
timeout 420
time 1999-03-24T10:00:00Z
wx fixture wx-2026-07-27T00Z.wxb

# CAMPAIGN W4, SORTIE 2 OF 10 - ALLIED FORCE 1999.
# THE SAME STRIKE UNDER A REAL CLOUD DECK - AND THE HONEST ANSWER IS "THE WIND".
# Spec, anchor and sources: doc/campaigns/w4-allied-force.md. Format: doc/missions/campaign.md.
# CONTROL: w4-01-floor.fbm - identical but for ONE line, `wx`, and the callsign prefix.
#
# THE ANCHOR: Lt Gen Michael C. Short, CFACC: "the stormy spring weather just kicked our butts for the
# first 45 days" [T3]; many crews came home with their bombs. Allied Force is the only campaign in this
# set whose WEATHER is as well documented as its order of battle, and W4's own §Knowledge 3 nominates
# this file and sortie 01 as the pair to build first, because they are one `wx` line apart and produce
# the number the cloud rebuild will be measured against.
#
# W4'S OWN SPEC PREDICTS THE ANSWER AND THIS FILE IS HERE TO PUT IT ON RECORD: "Does the deck change
# anything measurable? Expected answer today: no (C16 - cloud affects only the IRST). The mission
# exists so that the answer is on record before the cloud rebuild lands." Rule 7 says re-check a
# blocked mission against the TREE - and the re-check moves the sentence one notch: cloud reaches
# `sensors/FBVisualSystem` too (built 2026-07-28, the transmittance march through `core/FBCloudDensity`,
# doc/sensors.md 9.6c), which is the sensor that binds a MANPADS gunner and an optical gun. So the
# honest form of the prediction is: cloud changes nothing about a BOMB, and it can change something
# about an EYE. Sortie 03 is where the eye is in reach; here it is not.
#
# THE FIXTURE IS A JULY ANALYSIS FLOWN UNDER A MARCH CLOCK, and it is stated rather than hidden:
# `wx fixture` carries a GFS f000 analysis and has NO time axis (doc/missions/weather.md), so the
# atmosphere is a fixed field sampled at these coordinates and not a Balkan March. SAMPLED HERE
# (`build/fb-test-weather assets/wx-2026-07-27T00Z.wxb 42.70 20.90 4572`): total cover 75.8 %, mid
# 72.6 %, low 0 %, ceiling 6,861 m, visibility 19.1 km, wind 23.64 m/s from 272.4 deg = 46.0 kt.
# The deck sits ABOVE the floor here, which is itself the anchor's own problem: a 15,000 ft ingress
# under a mid deck is an ingress inside cloud.
#
# THE FIXTURE CARRIES TWO THINGS AT ONCE - CLOUD AND WIND - AND RULE 4 SAYS THAT GETS A CONTROL RUN
# RATHER THAN AN ARGUMENT. Attribution run A1 is this file with `wx wind 272 46`, i.e. the fixture's
# own 4,572 m wind restated as a closed form and no cloud at all. THE SEPARATION IS NOT CLEAN AND THE
# FILE SAYS SO BEFORE IT REPORTS: `wx wind` is ONE VECTOR at every altitude and the fixture is a
# PROFILE, so A1 minus 02 is cloud PLUS the profile. The campaign closes that hole with a sensitivity
# ladder rather than with an argument - see MEASURED.
#
# THE FOUR STRUCTURAL DISCLOSURES: see w4-01-floor.fbm. Unchanged here, and #3 is the one this file
# exists to measure.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: DOES A REAL 76 % DECK CHANGE ANYTHING MEASURABLE ABOUT A STRIKE?
#
# READING RULE (binding): exit 0 is the pass and it is not the answer. Read `stores DELIVERY` against
# 01's and against A1's, then count the `vis` lines (there are none to count on a jet with no aircraft
# to look at), then read `zone_sambelt_s`. A sortie that differs from its control ONLY by the wind is
# the finding, not a null result.
#
# MEASURED (fingerprint 89f1997ab141e9de, exit 3): THE DECK IS SCENERY AND THE WIND IS THE WEATHER.
#   01 (calm)                 `predErrM` 58.08   `aimErrM` **41.09 m**   `aimLongM` 36.80   target DESTROYED
#   02 (fixture: wind+cloud)  `predErrM` 275.4   `aimErrM` **257.30 m**  `aimLongM` 256.47  target INTACT
#   A1 (wind only, 272/46)    `predErrM` 304.2   `aimErrM` **284.15 m**  `aimLongM` 282.63  target INTACT
#   THE SENSITIVITY LADDER, run to turn the two-cause problem into an attribution instead of an
#   argument (rule 4) - this file with `wx wind 272 <kt>` and nothing else changed:
#     0 kt (= 01)  aimLongM  36.80 m      30 kt  aimLongM 192.81 m
#     10 kt        aimLongM 102.13 m      40 kt  aimLongM 246.38 m
#     20 kt        aimLongM 153.62 m      46 kt  aimLongM 282.63 m
#   The slope over 10-46 kt is **5.014 m of along-track error per knot** [DERIVED]. The fixture's own
#   release-altitude wind is 46.0 kt and it produces 256.47 m, which on that slope is the behaviour of
#   a constant **40.8 kt**: THE 26.2 m BY WHICH THE CONSTANT-WIND CONTROL EXCEEDS THE FIXTURE IS 5.2 kt
#   OF WIND PROFILE - the fixture decays from 23.64 m/s at 4,572 m to 8.54 m/s at 1,200 m over the same
#   point, and the bomb falls through all of it - AND IT IS NOT CLOUD.
#   THE CLOUD'S CONTRIBUTION IS STRUCTURALLY ZERO AND THE FILE SAYS SO RATHER THAN INFERRING IT: the
#   deck's only consumer in the tree is `sensors/FBVisualSystem`'s transmittance march, this file has
#   ONE aircraft and no visual engagement, and it logs **0 `vis` lines**. The fire control takes no
#   weather input at all, by design (doc/missions/weather.md: "the fire control gets no wind").
#   THE HONEST LIMIT, STATED: the campaign CANNOT separate cloud from wind by a control run, because
#   there is no "fixture without cloud" provider and `wx wind` is a single vector where the fixture is
#   a profile. What it can do is what it did - price the wind on its own ladder and show that the
#   residual is the profile - and point at the one geometry where the cloud does bite, which is sortie
#   07's transmittance of 8.0e-13 through a mid deck.
#   AND THE ANCHOR ARRIVES AS A NUMBER: under its own real atmosphere this campaign's unguided laydown
#   from the anchor's own altitude floor misses by 257 m and the target lives. Short's "the stormy
#   spring weather just kicked our butts" is, in this tree, not an abort - it is a miss.

zone flak 42.70000 20.98000 14000 0 3500
zone sambelt 42.70000 20.98000 14000 3500 8000

unit k2str
  module f16
  team friendly
  spawn 42.70000 20.60000 4572 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set datalink off
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk82
  set store 7 mk82
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  wp 42.70000 21.10000 4572 450
  wp 42.70000 20.70000 4572 450
  objective kill unit k2tgt
  objective survive
  objective avoid zone flak

unit k2man
  module sa7
  team hostile
  spawn 42.70000 21.06000 ground 270.0 0
  set emcon free
  set rounds 2

unit k2flk
  module zu23
  team hostile
  spawn 42.70000 21.09000 ground 270.0 0
  set emcon free
  set rounds 40

unit k2sam
  module sa6
  team hostile
  spawn 42.66000 20.98000 ground 270.0 0
  set emcon free
  set rounds 3

unit k2tgt
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 42.70000 21.10000 ground 90.0 0
